<title>ITALY: Fiat net pretax rise in first quarter 1997-Romiti.</title>
<headline>Fiat net pretax rise in first quarter 1997-Romiti.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial group Fiat's pre-tax consolidated profit was around 500 billion lire ($293.3 million) in the first quarter of 1997, group chairman Cesare Romiti said on Monday.</p>
<p>Romiti told the company's annual shareholders meeting that the first quarter results were an improvement on the previous quarter.</p>
<p>Group sales were 4.4 percent higher at 20.85 trillion lire in the first quarter, Romiti added.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321 ($ = 1705 Italian Lire)</p>
